Name: Rive Runtime and Rive Renderer
Short Name: rive
URL: https://github.com/rive-app/rive-runtime
Version: runtime-v0.1.747
Revision: 38fe8bb8360866a86b480d76363dc6494d858154
License: MIT
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Description:
Rive's C++ runtime (src/, include/, utils/, decoders/) and Rive Renderer, its
GPU renderer (renderer/), used by Cobalt's native <rive-player> element
(third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/rive/).

Only the GL backend of Rive Renderer is vendored (no D3D, Metal, Vulkan,
WebGPU or Ore). Scripting (src/lua) is not vendored. Layout uses Rive's Yoga
fork, vendored in //third_party/yoga.

renderer/generated_include/generated/shaders/ holds the minified shader
headers, generated once with upstream's script and Chromium's ply:
  cd renderer/src/shaders  # in an upstream checkout at the revision above
  make OUT=<out>/generated/shaders \
      FLAGS="-p <chromium>/src/third_party" minify
  cp <out>/generated/shaders/*.hpp <out>/generated/shaders/*.exports.h \
      renderer/generated_include/generated/shaders/

Local Modifications (marked "Cobalt patch"):
- include/rive/simple_array.hpp: include <cstdlib>.
- renderer/include/rive/renderer/gl/gles3.hpp: RIVE_CHROMIUM_GL, which calls
  GL through Chromium's GPU command buffer client (gles2_c_lib): headers,
  macros mapping GLES 3.x entry points to the names the command buffer
  exposes, and glDelete* wrappers that skip 0 (the client DCHECKs on it).
- renderer/src/gl/render_context_gl_impl.cpp: zero-initialize glGet* out
  params (the command buffer client DCHECKs that they are 0).
- cobalt/: Cobalt's interface to Rive Renderer (not upstream).
- BUILD.gn is Cobalt's own.
